{"id":"ara-t1-0001","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.eight","domain":2,"text_native":"ثمانية","text_romanized":"thamaaniya","text_english":"Eight.","source_caption":"8","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0002","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.five","domain":2,"text_native":"خمسة","text_romanized":"khamsa","text_english":"Five.","source_caption":"5","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Five is where most of these languages change to a different counting pattern, and knowing that in advance is the point of learning them in order.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0003","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.four","domain":2,"text_native":"اربعة","text_romanized":"arba`a","text_english":"Four.","source_caption":"4","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0004","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.nine","domain":2,"text_native":"تسعة","text_romanized":"tis`a","text_english":"Nine.","source_caption":"9","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0005","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.one","domain":2,"text_native":"واحد","text_romanized":"waaHid","text_english":"One.","source_caption":"1","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Counting from one upward in order, because a traveller counts by reciting rather than by arithmetic.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0006","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.seven","domain":2,"text_native":"سبعة","text_romanized":"sab`a","text_english":"Seven.","source_caption":"7","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0007","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.six","domain":2,"text_native":"ستة","text_romanized":"sitta","text_english":"Six.","source_caption":"6","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0008","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.ten","domain":2,"text_native":"عشرة","text_romanized":"`ashara","text_english":"Ten.","source_caption":"10","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The first number past the counting pattern in most of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0009","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.three","domain":2,"text_native":"ثلاثة","text_romanized":"thalaatha","text_english":"Three.","source_caption":"3","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0010","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.two","domain":2,"text_native":"إثنان","text_romanized":"ithnaan","text_english":"Two.","source_caption":"2","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0011","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"count.zero","domain":2,"text_native":"صفر","text_romanized":"Sifr","text_english":"None, zero.","source_caption":"0","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Zero is the answer that gets misheard most often, because the word for nothing and the word for a small quantity are often unrelated.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0012","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"price.how-much","domain":3,"text_native":"بكم","text_romanized":"biKam","text_english":"How much is this?","source_caption":"How much?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most useful question in the tier, and the one people are most afraid to ask. It is not rude anywhere.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0013","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-cheap","domain":3,"text_native":"رخيص","text_romanized":"rakhees","text_english":"It is cheaper in my country.","source_caption":"cheap","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Read as an accusation almost everywhere. Included because knowing that it is an accusation is worth more than being able to say it politely.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0014","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-expensive","domain":3,"text_native":"غالي","text_romanized":"ghali","text_english":"That is too expensive.","source_caption":"expensive","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used with the hand gesture that accompanies it. The gesture carries the meaning and the word confirms it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0015","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"toilet.where","domain":12,"text_native":"اين الحمام؟","text_romanized":"ayn al-Hammaam?","text_english":"Where is the toilet?","source_caption":"Where is the toilet?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most urgent question in this tier and the one every phrasebook leads with. In several languages the word is the only one a traveller needs for years.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0016","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"food.water","domain":4,"text_native":"ماء","text_romanized":"maa'","text_english":"Water, please.","source_caption":"water","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing the water in a restaurant is a small discourtesy in several of these countries. This is how to ask for some instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0017","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"way.straight","domain":7,"text_native":"على طول Ala Tool (Egyptian) or illal amaama الى الامام; dughri (Jordan); quduman","text_romanized":"general","text_english":"Go straight ahead.","source_caption":"straight ahead","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0018","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-left","domain":7,"text_native":"لف يسار","text_romanized":"lif yassar","text_english":"Turn left.","source_caption":"Turn left","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced: you are the one being given directions far more often than giving them.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0019","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-right","domain":7,"text_native":"لف يمين","text_romanized":"lif yameen","text_english":"Turn right.","source_caption":"Turn right","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0020","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"health.doctor","domain":9,"text_native":"احتاج دكتر a","text_romanized":"Htaaj duktur","text_english":"I need a doctor.","source_caption":"I need a doctor.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Short enough to say to anyone, which is the point — a phrase you cannot finish is a phrase that arrives too late.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0021","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"health.hurt","domain":9,"text_native":"إنني مصاب","text_romanized":"innani muSabun","text_english":"I have been injured.","source_caption":"I've been injured.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Declares the situation before being asked. Several of these languages change tense or register on the word for injury, and the flat version sounds like a complaint.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0022","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"help.dont-touch","domain":10,"text_native":"ما تلمسني","text_romanized":"ma tilmisni","text_english":"Do not touch me.","source_caption":"Don't touch me!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Out loud and to a person, not shouted generally. Several of these languages treat it as an accusation, so it is a sentence to use deliberately.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0023","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"help.emergency","domain":10,"text_native":"طوارئ","text_romanized":"Taware","text_english":"It is an emergency.","source_caption":"It's an emergency.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Changes how the next thirty seconds go. Two words, and in several of these languages it reaches a different set of responses than a request would.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0024","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"help.leave-me-alone","domain":10,"text_native":"اتركني / اتركيني","text_romanized":"utrukni","text_english":"Please leave me alone.","source_caption":"Leave me alone.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said firmly and quietly. Raising the volume is what turns it from a boundary into an incident in several of these cultures.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0025","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"help.lost","domain":10,"text_native":"أضعت طريقي a","text_romanized":"da'tu tareeqi","text_english":"I am lost.","source_caption":"I'm lost.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking a passer-by for help is a separate skill from reading a sign, and it uses different vocabulary in every one of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0026","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"help.phone","domain":10,"text_native":"هل ممكن استخدم التلفون؟","text_romanized":"Hal mumkin astakhdim at-tilifun?","text_english":"Can I use your phone?","source_caption":"Can I use your phone?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most common thing a traveller needs that a phone provides, and asking a stranger for it is usually granted.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0027","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"help.police","domain":10,"text_native":"سأتصل بالشرطة","text_romanized":"sa'ataSal bashurTah","text_english":"Please call the police.","source_caption":"I'll call the police.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Usually needs a phone, and in most places a local number rather than an international one.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"ara-t1-0028","lang":"ara","tier":1,"slot":"help.thief","domain":10,"text_native":"!توقف! السارق","text_romanized":"tawqaf! assaariq","text_english":"Stop, thief!","source_caption":"Stop! Thief!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Loud, and aimed at a crowd rather than at one person. Included because the vocabulary exists and because it is the sentence that makes people nearby move.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Arabic phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Arabic_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
